* Account\nabstraction
** Where it sits
*** ERC-4337\nabove the protocol,\nEOAs still exist
*** Aztec\nin the protocol,\nno EOAs at all
*** 4337 needs an\nalt mempool and\nbundlers
*** Aztec needs neither
** Validation and DoS
*** 4337 restricts\nwhat validation may do\nopcodes, storage, gas
*** Aztec proves validation\nclient-side
*** Sequencer verifies a\nconstant-size proof
*** Complex validation\ncosts the network nothing
** Keys
*** 4337 rotates\neverything
*** Aztec signing key\nrotatable, app-defined
*** Nullifier and viewing\nkeys are fixed\nin the address
*** Recovery cannot\nrestore note access
** Addresses
*** 4337 CREATE2\nfactory + initCode
*** Aztec hash of\npublic keys and\npartial address
*** Both counterfactual
*** Complete address\nneeded to spend
** Nonces
*** 4337 semi-abstracted\n192-bit key +\n64-bit sequence
*** EntryPoint still\nenforces it
*** Aztec fully abstracted\nno protocol nonce
*** Sequential, unordered,\ntime-windowed, Merkle
** Fees
*** 4337 paymaster\nwith EntryPoint\ndeposit and stake
*** Aztec fee-paying\ncontract in the\nteardown phase
*** Fee Juice is\nnon-transferable
*** Sponsored, private\nand third-party FPC
** Delegated\nauthorisation
*** ERC-20 approve\nblanket allowance
*** Authwit authorises\none exact action
*** Nullifier makes\nit single-use
*** Cancel by emitting\nthe nullifier
*** Does not grant\naccess to note secrets
@endmindmap
